<%# FUIME: why this venture cannot sell, shown to the people who can fix it.

    The mirror image of the public storefront, which deliberately says nothing.
    These strings name operators and state their ages, so this partial belongs
    only on authenticated pages the operator or their guardian can see — never on
    a public URL. See Event#selling_blockers.

    Renders nothing when there is nothing wrong, so it is safe to drop at the top
    of any venture page.

    Usage: render "fuime/selling_blockers", event: @event
    Optional: blockers: (defaults to event.offer_publish_blockers), title:

    The usage line above is deliberately NOT written as ERB. An `<%%=` escape
    still carries a `%>`, and a `<%#` comment ends at the FIRST `%>` it meets —
    so the remainder of this block closed early and the trailing `%>` was printed
    to the page, as literal text, above the callout. It was visible on the offer
    wizard's review step: the last screen a teenager reads before publishing. %>

<% blockers = local_assigns.fetch(:blockers) { event.offer_publish_blockers } %>

<%# The caller's title, when there is one. Every call site passed `title:` and
    this partial ignored it, so the offer wizard asked "Ready to publish?" and
    was answered "This business can't take payments yet" — a bigger, more
    alarming statement than the one the caller meant, on a venture whose only
    problem was that the review had not run yet. %>
<% callout_title = local_assigns.fetch(:title, "This business can't take payments yet") %>

<% if blockers.any? %>
  <%= render "application/callout", type: "warning", title: callout_title do %>
    <ul class="mb-2 pl-4">
      <% blockers.each do |blocker| %>
        <li><%= blocker %></li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>

    <p class="mb-0 text-sm muted">
      <%# The two states differ in who has to act, and saying so saves a support
          email: "not approved yet" is Fuime's move, everything else is theirs. %>
      <% if event.operator_vetting_unvetted? %>
        We'll do a quick review before you go live. You can keep drafting —
        we'll email you when you can publish.
      <% else %>
        Once these are sorted, your payment page starts working again.
        <%= help_message %>
      <% end %>
    </p>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
